    "narrative": "For today\u2019s Independence Day slate, the analytics office is leaning heavily into the favorable matchup for **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Tyler Freeman** (72.83). **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against Alcantara, where a combination of park factors and a plus platoon advantage drives his score to the top of our board. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** thrives in his matchup against Ray; despite the veteran presence on the mound, the combination of a hitter-friendly park and a #4 lineup spot cements him as an elite play. **Luis Arraez** also presents significant upside (69.53) today, as he faces a soft matchup against Sullivan with high projected park efficiency, making him a high-floor anchor for our batting average category.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with **Daulton Varsho** (47.69) and **Yainer Diaz** (40.31). **Daulton Varsho** faces a stiff test against the high-quality arm of Gilbert, and while his platoon edge provides some mitigation, his efficiency remains suppressed by the pitcher\u2019s skill level. **Yainer Diaz** is currently riding the lower end of our starting threshold; despite being a primary option, the tough matchup against Rasmussen makes him our most marginal start. The most difficult bench decision was **Taylor Ward** (41.87), who missed the cut strictly due to higher aggregate efficiency scores from the rest of the outfield corps; his projected output against a decent Greene suggests he is a high-quality reserve should a late scratch occur elsewhere.\n\nFinally, managers should monitor the situation with **Bryson Stott** (64.54). While he is a strong play based on his platoon edge against Wacha, he carries a 40% rain risk alert, which could compromise his game-capping value. Additionally, we are tracking **Gavin Sheets** (46.35); as his lineup spot remains pending, his score is currently modeled on a #4 projection, which may fluctuate if his actual batting order slides down. We remain thin in the infield due to the absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman** on the IL, placing additional pressure on **Jonathan Aranda** and **Geraldo Perdomo** to maintain production levels while our secondary prospects like **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Drew Gilbert** remain in reserve readiness.",
